1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,533
What if, right now… you could see exactly what was going to

2
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:08,433
happen in the next 10 seconds? What would you do? Avoid an

3
00:00:08,433 --> 00:00:12,367
embarrassing fall? Prevent an accident? Find out what your crush is about

4
00:00:12,367 --> 00:00:16,300
to say? Or… use those 10 seconds to change something you might

5
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:20,200
regret for the rest of your life? It sounds like a pretty

6
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:24,133
small superpower. But think about it. Ten seconds can sometimes change everything.

7
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:29,433
The rule is simple. Whenever you focus and blink… you can see

8
00:00:29,433 --> 00:00:33,567
exactly 10 seconds into the future. Not a feeling. Not a prediction. You

9
00:00:33,567 --> 00:00:37,400
actually see what is about to happen. Then… you return to the

10
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:41,200
present. And you have 10 seconds to decide: let that future happen…

11
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:45,333
or try to change it. At first? You would obviously use this incredible

12
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:49,167
power for the most important things in life. Like… not embarrassing yourself.

13
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:55,033
You see yourself trip. And somehow… the entire cup of coffee ends

14
00:00:55,033 --> 00:00:59,067
up all over your clothes. Even worse… someone nearby is already

15
00:00:59,067 --> 00:01:03,500
holding a phone. No. The internet does not need another meme today.

16
00:01:03,533 --> 00:01:07,000
You return to the present. Step slightly to the left.

17
00:01:07,033 --> 00:01:09,800
Avoid the crack. Perfect. You smile

18
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:12,567
confidently. Having a superpower feels amazing.

19
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:15,700
Then… you walk straight into a pole. BONK!

20
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,167
Apparently… seeing the future still cannot save your dignity.

21
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:24,300
During a meeting… you suddenly see your boss calling your

22
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:28,400
name. You have exactly 10 seconds. Your brain instantly enters emergency

23
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:32,467
mode. You open the document. Scan the most important line. Ten

24
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:36,167
seconds later… “What do you think?” You sit up straight.

25
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:39,633
Stay calm. And give a surprisingly intelligent answer.

26
00:01:39,633 --> 00:01:43,533
Everyone nods. Your boss looks impressed. Congratulations. You just

27
00:01:43,533 --> 00:01:46,967
used a supernatural ability to look like someone…

28
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,433
who was actually paying attention during the meeting. And honestly…

29
00:01:50,433 --> 00:01:54,200
that might be one of the best uses of this power.

30
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:00,167
Sometimes the power would help with much smaller things. You see your phone

31
00:02:00,167 --> 00:02:05,100
about to fall off the table. The screen hits the floor. Shatters. You return

32
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:09,667
to the present. Calmly reach out your hand. The cat pushes the phone.

33
00:02:09,667 --> 00:02:14,600
And… you catch it. Perfect. Your superpower just saved you a few hundred dollars

34
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:19,167
in repairs. But from this point on… things start getting much more serious.

35
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:23,233
You are about to cross the street.

36
00:02:23,267 --> 00:02:27,733
The light is green. Everything looks completely normal. Then you

37
00:02:27,733 --> 00:02:32,633
blink. And see… a vehicle speeding out from a blind corner.

38
00:02:32,667 --> 00:02:38,167
If you keep moving… you are going to collide. You return to the present.

39
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:43,433
And stop. One second. Two seconds. Three. The vehicle actually flies past

40
00:02:43,433 --> 00:02:48,233
you. Only a few feet away. And for the first time…

41
00:02:48,267 --> 00:02:53,600
you realize something. This power is not just useful for avoiding

42
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:58,967
embarrassing moments. It could save your life. Maybe even someone else’s.

43
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:05,733
And of course… you would immediately think about sports. During a game… you see

44
00:03:05,733 --> 00:03:10,833
your opponent move to the right. Easy. You return to the present… and move

45
00:03:10,833 --> 00:03:15,933
right before he even makes his move. But there is a problem. He sees

46
00:03:15,933 --> 00:03:21,067
you move. So he changes direction. Left. Wait. That is not what you saw.

47
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:25,333
And that is when you discover the biggest problem with your

48
00:03:25,333 --> 00:03:29,967
power. The future is not fixed. The moment you change what you

49
00:03:29,967 --> 00:03:34,200
do… the future changes too. Every decision creates a different outcome.

50
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:39,933
During a job interview… you see the next question. “What

51
00:03:39,933 --> 00:03:44,267
is your biggest weakness?” You have 10 seconds to prepare.

52
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:46,667
This time… no awkward silence.

53
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:49,833
No panic. You deliver the perfect answer.

54
00:03:49,867 --> 00:03:54,767
The interviewer smiles. But then you look 10 seconds ahead again.

55
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:59,133
And hear him ask: “Did you prepare that answer beforehand?” …

56
00:03:59,167 --> 00:04:04,000
Okay. Maybe this power cannot save you from every interview.

57
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:10,467
But some things are much harder. You are standing in front of

58
00:04:10,467 --> 00:04:15,300
someone you have liked for months. The words have been stuck in

59
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:20,567
your head forever. You blink. And see her reaction. “I’m sorry…” Your heart

60
00:04:20,567 --> 00:04:25,433
drops. Now you have a choice. You could stay silent. Say nothing.

61
00:04:25,467 --> 00:04:30,733
Never get rejected. Never feel the pain. But then you start thinking…

62
00:04:30,767 --> 00:04:33,767
if you avoid every future you do not

63
00:04:33,767 --> 00:04:37,167
like… are you really living? You take a breath.

64
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:42,600
And say it anyway. “I like you.” She pauses. Then… “I’m sorry. I’m

65
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:48,033
just not ready for a relationship.” Exactly what you saw. But this time…

66
00:04:48,033 --> 00:04:53,867
you smile. Because at least now… you have an answer. Some futures do not

67
00:04:53,867 --> 00:04:59,267
need to be changed. Sometimes… you just need enough courage to face them.

68
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:05,067
Then one day… those 10 seconds really change you. Your phone

69
00:05:05,067 --> 00:05:09,533
starts ringing. It is your mom. You are busy. You think:

70
00:05:09,533 --> 00:05:14,433
“I’ll call her back later.” Your finger moves toward the decline button.

71
00:05:14,433 --> 00:05:18,900
But out of habit… you look 10 seconds into the future.

72
00:05:18,933 --> 00:05:23,967
You see yourself rejecting the call. Walking forward. And behind you… an

73
00:05:23,967 --> 00:05:29,400
elderly man steps into the road. A truck is coming straight toward him.

74
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:34,400
You return to the present. You do not think. You run. Grab

75
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:39,833
the man. Pull him backward. The truck flies past. Missing both of you

76
00:05:39,833 --> 00:05:44,867
by inches. You are breathing hard. The man does not even understand

77
00:05:44,867 --> 00:05:49,867
what just happened. You just saved someone’s life. Then… your phone vibrates

78
00:05:49,867 --> 00:05:55,300
again. Your mom is still calling. You answer. “Mom?” There is a brief

79
00:05:55,300 --> 00:06:00,333
silence. Then she simply asks: “Did you eat yet?” That is it.

80
00:06:00,367 --> 00:06:05,833
No emergency. No terrible news. No dramatic final words. Just an

81
00:06:05,833 --> 00:06:11,267
ordinary question. The kind of question you might ignore every day.

82
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:15,600
You laugh. “Yeah, Mom. I already ate.” You talk for

83
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:20,300
a few minutes. Nothing dramatic happens. But suddenly… you realize something.

84
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:25,000
You spent the entire day staring 10 seconds into the future…

85
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:29,300
and nearly ignored someone who was with you… right now.

86
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:33,933
You thought the greatest part of your power…

87
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:37,000
was knowing what would happen next.

88
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:42,400
But it was not. Because even if you can see 10 seconds ahead…

89
00:06:42,567 --> 00:06:46,900
you still do not know what happens in 10 minutes.

90
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:52,033
Tomorrow. Next year. Or when the last time you see someone…

91
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:54,867
will actually be. And maybe…

92
00:06:55,067 --> 00:06:58,833
that is exactly what gives life its meaning.

93
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:05,967
Of course… seeing 10 seconds into the future is only a thought experiment.

94
00:07:05,967 --> 00:07:11,333
It is not something we can actually do. In real life… there is

95
00:07:11,333 --> 00:07:16,300
no rewind button. No warning screen. No countdown telling us that an

96
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:21,667
important moment is about to happen. But maybe… we do not need one.

97
00:07:21,667 --> 00:07:27,033
You can still look before crossing the street. You can still say what

98
00:07:27,033 --> 00:07:32,400
you really feel. You can call your parents. Apologize to someone. Thank someone.

99
00:07:32,433 --> 00:07:36,567
Hold someone you love for a little longer. And sometimes…

100
00:07:36,567 --> 00:07:40,700
small decisions like those are enough to change the future.

101
00:07:40,733 --> 00:07:44,400
You do not need to see 10 seconds ahead to

102
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:48,100
live a better life. You just need to stop wasting…

103
00:07:48,133 --> 00:07:52,667
the 10 seconds you have right now. “The future can wait. This

104
00:07:52,667 --> 00:07:57,167
moment can’t.” If you really could see 10 seconds into the future…

105
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:59,233
what would you use it for?
